    ("technical", "easy", 120, ["structural"],
     "What is the difference between dead load, live load and wind load, and why do we apply load factors?",
     "Dead load is permanent self-weight; live load is occupancy and movable load; wind load is lateral environmental load. Load factors cover uncertainty in loads and the consequence of failure; the structure is checked for the worst combinations under limit-state design."),
